# shadcn/ui Best Practices

- Official references:
  - https://ui.shadcn.com/
  - https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components
  - https://ui.shadcn.com/docs

- Treat shadcn/ui as open code: prefer updating local components in `components/ui/*` instead of building parallel wrappers without clear need.
- Reuse existing primitives first (`Button`, `Input`, `Dialog`, etc.) before creating new UI components.
- Follow composition patterns (`asChild`, Radix `Slot`, `data-slot` attributes) to keep APIs consistent and accessible.
- Use `class-variance-authority` variants for visual states and sizes; avoid ad-hoc class duplication across features.
- Keep styling token-based and consistent with project design tokens/utilities; avoid one-off hardcoded values unless justified.
- Preserve accessibility defaults (keyboard interaction, focus states, aria attributes) when customizing components.
- When adding or changing a component API, keep it minimal and consistent with existing shadcn component patterns in this repo.
